# Naming conventions

Living standards — refine as the domain grows. Prefer clear **hauling / mission** words: `Session`, `Mission`, `ChecklistItem`, `Player`, `HaulingPayload`.

## Files & folders

| Kind | Convention | Examples |
| --- | --- | --- |
| App routes | Next.js defaults; folders `kebab-case` only when multi-word | `app/api/health/db/route.ts` |
| Components | `PascalCase.tsx` | `Button.tsx`, `MissionPanel.tsx` |
| Hooks | `use` + `PascalCase` feature → file `useThing.ts` | `useSessionBundle.ts` |
| Lib / utils | `camelCase.ts` or domain folder + `camelCase` | `lib/missions/types.ts` |
| DB | `db/schema.ts`, `db/queries/<domain>.ts` | `db/queries/sessions.ts` |
| Stories | Co-locate `ComponentName.stories.tsx` or `stories/foundation/` | `Panel.stories.tsx` |
| CSS / globals | keep `app/globals.css`; avoid random style sheets | — |
| Env example | `.env.example` | — |

Folders for features: short **plural domain** names when grouping (`components/ui`, `lib/missions`, `db/queries`).

## React components

- **PascalCase** for components and their files: `ChecklistItemRow`, `SessionHeader`.
- Props types: `ComponentNameProps` (`MissionCardProps`).
- One primary export per component file; story file shares the name.

## Hooks

- `use` + PascalCase: `useMissionProgress`, `useSessionPlayers`.
- Custom hook files match the export name.

## Server actions / API

- Route handlers stay in `route.ts` (Next convention).
- Exported handlers: framework names (`GET`, `POST`, …).
- Helper functions: **verb + domain**, `camelCase` — `createSessionWithOwner`, `addHaulingMission`, `upsertChecklistItem`.
- Prefer `db/queries/*` names that read as use-cases, not raw SQL verbs alone.

## DB models & fields (Drizzle)

- **Tables:** `plural` `snake_case` in Postgres; Drizzle exports **camelCase plurals** matching domain: `sessions`, `players`, `missions`, `sessionPlayers`, `checklistProgress`.
- **Columns:** Drizzle property **camelCase** (`joinCode`, `displayName`, `sortOrder`); SQL column `snake_case` via the column helper string.
- **Enums:** Drizzle `xxxEnum` + SQL name `snake_case` — `missionTypeEnum` → `mission_type`; values **lowercase** / `snake_case` strings: `hauling`, `planned`, `owner`.
- Inferred types: `Mission`, `Session`, `Player`, `ChecklistProgress` (singular PascalCase).

## JSON payload types

- Payload interfaces/types: **PascalCase** + clear suffix — `HaulingMissionPayload`, `ChecklistTemplateItem`, `MissionLocation`.
- Discriminator field: `kind` (string literal, e.g. `"hauling"`).
- Checklist keys in JSON: **`snake_case` or `kebab-case` stable IDs** — prefer `snake_case` string keys: `load_cargo`, `turn_in` (not UI labels).
- Type guards / factories: `isHaulingPayload`, `emptyHaulingPayload`.

## Env vars

- **SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE**: `DATABASE_URL`.
- Server-only; no `NEXT_PUBLIC_` unless the value is intentionally public.
- Document every var in `.env.example`.

## CSS / design tokens

- CSS variables: `--rsi-*` **kebab-case** after the prefix — `--rsi-bg`, `--rsi-text-secondary`, `--rsi-accent`.
- Tailwind utilities from `@theme`: `rsi-*` — `bg-rsi-surface`, `text-rsi-accent`.
- Do not invent parallel token prefixes (`--color-brand-*` etc.) without updating the theme rule.

## Booleans

- Props / fields: affirmative prefixes — `is`, `has`, `can`, `should` — `isCompleted` in TS; DB column `completed` is OK when it is the stored fact.
- Avoid negations (`isNotReady`); prefer `isReady` and invert at use site.

## Constants

- Module-level immutable values: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE` for true constants (`DEFAULT_JOIN_CODE_LENGTH`), or `camelCase` for config objects (`defaultHaulingChecklist`).
- Prefer colocating domain defaults next to types (`emptyHaulingPayload`).

## Enums

- Prefer Drizzle `pgEnum` / string-union types over numeric enums.
- TypeScript union or const object: values **lowercase** domain strings (`"active"`, `"hauling"`).
- Const maps: `PascalCase` type name + `camelCase` object if needed (`missionStatusValues`).

## Domain vocabulary (prefer these)

| Use | Avoid |
| --- | --- |
| `Session` | `Room`, `Lobby`, `Game` |
| `Player` | `User` (until auth exists), `Member` alone |
| `Mission` | `Job`, `Quest`, `Task` (task = checklist step) |
| `ChecklistItem` / `itemKey` | `Todo`, `StepId` without context |
| `Hauling` / `hauling` | `Delivery` as the type name (delivery can be a checklist group) |
| `payload` | `data`, `json`, `blob` for mission body |

Refine this list in PRs; update this file when the team agrees on new terms.
